===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[physically|Physically]] [[broken]] into [[pieces]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1907|author=[[w:Harold Edward Bindloss|Harold Bindloss]]
|title=The Dust of Conflict
|chapter=30|url=http://openlibrary.org/works/OL4429277W
|passage=It was by his order the '''shattered''' leading company flung itself into the houses when the Sin Verguenza were met by an enfilading volley as they reeled into the calle.}}
# [[emotionally|Emotionally]] [[defeated]] or [[dispirited]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2000|author=Lionel Robbins|title=A history of economic thought: the LSE lectures|page=221|publisher=Princeton University Press
|passage=Well, she died after seven years of marriage, and Mill thought that he was '''shattered''', and '''shattered''' no doubt he was, in the sense of this absolutely irreparable emotional loss.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2000|author=Nellie McHenry|title=Forbidden Dreams of Love,|chapter=26
|passage=She refused to see him for two days. He was '''shattered'''. He sent his apologies.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2010|author=Mary Alice Beasley|title=Shattered Lens: A Tale of Domestic Violence and Redemption Through Love|page=261|publisher=AuthorHouse
|passage=Yes, he had gotten his revenge for my rejection. I was '''shattered''' but remained silent.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|author={{w|Dia Frampton}}|title=The Broken Ones|album={{w|Red (Dia Frampton album)|Red}}|year=2011|artist={{w|Dia Frampton}}|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Zz04teo1j9k|text=And oh, maybe I see a part of me in them / The missing piece, always trying to fit in / The '''shattered''' heart, hungry for a home / No, you're not alone / I love the broken ones}}
# {{lb|en|British|colloquial}} Extremely [[tired]] or [[exhausted]].
#: {{ux|en|I stayed up all night working, and now I'm completely '''shattered'''.}}

